{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:27:30.759951Z","id":"15dd1dff62806a5ca13a8ae6fdbf55f546b0d6f72881b17649fd112ae5b6c9ea","body":{"detail":"Measured under wrangler dev --local: POST /do/demo/fill?mb=4 wrote 1034 chunks in one commit in about 100 ms. Durable Object SQL bills per row written and caps a row at 2 MB, so a larger chunk (say 64 KiB, with PRAGMA page_size up to 65536) would cut rows and JS crossings for bulk writes at the cost of write amplification for small transactions. CHUNK_SIZE in crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs is the knob; measure with Clax's real write mix before changing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"7b1819560acf103f31ced6bdd13ead48afd91732fb99ae8f9c73bced08a21341"},"summary":"Each commit runs one ctx.storage.sql.exec per 4 KiB chunk: a 4 MiB transaction is ~1034 statements and rows written","tags":["vfs","performance","cost","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:27:30.760085Z","id":"c769c2b64da663d492d3958594fb4a3538a9807d4807269a467813220984b6b9","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":253},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"600260720dd160c58afa020bcb7a4620ee34abf151dcab03b6efb1b7b83bdbfa"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:35.580813Z","id":"c8f34b5e034071adb386a3b68a8d651997b11bc6404e4857c31560bc3c6e671d","body":{"detail":"StoredFile keeps every chunk a transaction writes in dirty (crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs:173:192) until commit, and commit copies all of them into JS arrays (lines 160:166) before the storage transaction starts. A 50 MB publish therefore needs about 100 MB at once, plus SQLite's page cache (sqlite-wasm-rs 0.5.5 builds with SQLITE_DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE=-16384, 16 MiB) and the memory journal of overwritten pages, against an isolate limit of 128 MB (developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits) that every Durable Object in the isolate shares. Wasm memory never shrinks, so the high-water mark stays for the isolate's life. Per-row (2 MB), statement (100 KB) and bound-parameter (100) limits of DO SQL are met by 4 KiB chunks and 3 parameters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"6a6342969567ecde8ab1515d370c513c9e687c1d041fae7eec95b8a2b2953f7c"},"suggested_fix":"Create each Uint8Array inside the transactionSync callback from a dirty map moved into it (restored on failure), set PRAGMA cache_size for the isolate budget, and keep large artifact bodies out of the SQLite file (R2, or rows of their own in DO storage) with a size cap on one transaction.","summary":"A large transaction holds about twice its size in memory at commit: the dirty set in wasm memory plus a Uint8Array copy of every chunk made before transactionSync","tags":["vfs","memory","limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.771174Z","id":"e453d2c8ffe67539331ced41583cf3b8c28dec441d0a0a4543fd89bbcbd1549a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0bf47593","summary":"Fixed in 0bf47593: DoPageStore::commit makes each chunk's Uint8Array inside the transactionSync callback, reading the dirty set through an Rc the VFS takes back after the commit, so no second copy of the transaction is built up front; open() sets cache_size from Limits::cache_bytes (8 MiB by default); a write past Limits::max_transaction_bytes (16 MiB by default) fails with SQLITE_FULL and the transaction rolls back. Evidence (cargo test --workspace in crates/clax-worker: adversarial 13 passed, 0 ignored; vfs 5 passed): a_transaction_past_the_cap_fails_and_rolls_back passes for a spilling and an at-commit transaction (SQLITE_FULL, rows and stored bytes unchanged, integrity ok, the next commit stored); node crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs prints 'ok   a 17 MiB transaction fails at the 16 MiB cap'. The memory figures are estimates: see the concern on Limits::default.","supersedes":"c8f34b5e034071adb386a3b68a8d651997b11bc6404e4857c31560bc3c6e671d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.780642Z","id":"0fba429061d99ebf3bffe74f5beb9ff16c2e1ae5ba7b268f3e212d554b62a51f","body":{"detail":"Measured under wrangler dev --local: POST /do/demo/fill?mb=4 wrote 1034 chunks in one commit in about 100 ms. Durable Object SQL bills per row written and caps a row at 2 MB, so a larger chunk (say 64 KiB, with PRAGMA page_size up to 65536) would cut rows and JS crossings for bulk writes at the cost of write amplification for small transactions. CHUNK_SIZE in crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs is the knob; measure with Clax's real write mix before changing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"e0a97a76a1064838836af290cf6a39a2c3722ab3ed423ae74257f973d3a9b7b4"},"summary":"Each commit runs one ctx.storage.sql.exec per 4 KiB chunk: a 4 MiB transaction is ~1034 statements and rows written","supersedes":"15dd1dff62806a5ca13a8ae6fdbf55f546b0d6f72881b17649fd112ae5b6c9ea","tags":["vfs","performance","cost","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.782602Z","id":"03b5bcf097345e4cc73a2057082676a8e6d2f762c6c5a20718d49fde001e6c89","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":288},"content_hash":"d143dd5ab7307c9179917744c58a2db137300422d33694b710645ac9772bb751"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"c769c2b64da663d492d3958594fb4a3538a9807d4807269a467813220984b6b9","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819348Z","id":"152eccb222f89af0b7eb19d266d222468db35a878ba2f2c285525679eab009ae","body":{"detail":"With conn_of None (crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs), GET /api/token answers 403 not_loopback and the owner and events cookies never count, so the owner is only whoever presents CLAX_TOKEN as a bearer token (scripts, agents), never a browser. Anyone who reaches the Worker gets a clax_viewer cookie and, as on a daemon bound to the LAN, reads every artifact and comments (people are not filtered: feedback::VisFor). bind is 127.0.0.1 here, so invites answer 409 not_on_lan; browser_base and self_base are PUBLIC_ORIGIN or http://localhost; codex push, sampling and the audit journal are off; extension_id is empty, so the Chrome extension cannot pair. What hosted mode (the rust-hosted-signin branch) must change: a sign-in that makes a browser the owner or a person (an owner credential that does not depend on the peer), refusing anonymous viewers on a public deploy, invites without a LAN address, and the public host as browser_base.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"d9930b39ce91d40c48fa887a8452253e1a1c018423730b09bf677cef8c85acff"},"summary":"On the Worker every browser is a LAN viewer and no browser can become the owner: hosted mode must replace these local semantics","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819386Z","id":"559b60dd40fe42bb90375cc02208bcb68bb9eeb4295859960e2bd835acd43501","body":{"detail":"InstanceDo::alarm runs AppState::sweep and re-arms at SWEEP_INTERVAL (5 s) whenever inst.sockets is non-empty, else every 60 s, forever, even for an idle instance. The sweeps mostly have nothing due: working records and presence expire on their own deadlines, detached streams after stream::GRACE, seats after their idle release. Suggested: compute the earliest due deadline from Working, Presence, the hub's detached index and LiveSeats, and set the alarm for that (none when nothing is due), plus the grant sweep's next expiry from the store.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"aaaa143bbc357a17accf10cf628c00ef4e6a1f85c1c2e68fdeab03e5721aefe5"},"suggested_fix":"Add a next_due() to AppState over the sweeps' deadlines and arm the alarm at it.","summary":"The alarm fires every 5 s while any socket is open, which wakes a hibernated object every 5 s and so undoes most of what hibernation saves","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819420Z","id":"14d2d0a067f2f8a886782f40f2effacba9d06ebd3b697e539ef4fe45789e35f7","body":{"detail":"Not served on the Worker: GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/room (the room capability's socket; routes/room.rs is native only and its frames ride per-room tokio broadcast receivers that need a drain of their own, see 61069320), /mcp (the JSON-RPC adapter of crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs, not built), GET /api/events (SSE). Not run: the session reaper (daemon::reap_idle checks local PIDs), the stale check and the audit journal. Still on a timer: a question's grace (questions::start_grace, see dfae291e), which keeps the object awake and is lost at eviction. After a wake the hub, live seats and presence start empty: each socket gets a new stream and the shell subscribes again, so seats are taken again in that order and presence chips disappear until tabs report (102650cd). There is no live-layers socket on this base to carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"953bc48adec794617647e9f306821728dc085b7332143ade237d2b111b6329df"},"summary":"What the daemon runs that the Worker does not: rooms, /mcp, the session reaper, question graces on a timer, live seats and presence across a wake","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819520Z","id":"b36a16b82268f582575348b72709054d2c51eb2fbc81b04f1b7e0836670dc25b","body":{"detail":"It stands in for the git backend (one repository per artifact) that a parallel branch builds, behind crates/clax-worker/src/content.rs content_store (CLAX_CONTENT=storage|memory). It works with the store's synchronous paths because SQL storage calls finish when first polled; a GitContent whose reads are promises will panic in clax_core::content::wait until the content handlers await the async methods (1eeb8d87). All content shares the object's storage limit and its single thread; a file up to MAX_FILE_BYTES is copied into wasm memory on each read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"844b8e94e6d64ed6db653d61feb3c19649a71c15693ecb925e3bcfc8dd894a8c"},"summary":"DoContent keeps every version file of the instance in one Durable Object's SQL storage, read whole into memory per request","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819567Z","id":"6699046dc1f9b7ff717a8eb2406bf2e0f2bb96b7121915da9f60c957c653f3d5","body":{"detail":"Anyone who reaches the Worker can create spike objects and write notes or 16 MiB of blobs into them (POST /do/{name}/fill). test-wasm.mjs depends on them. Before any deploy they need to go behind CLAX_TEST_ROUTES (as /_worker/hibernate is) or into a Worker of their own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"0101458254fd690eb76a5b19da536eb2e4a4ab6d87cc78507b85bbc3f5dda7a3"},"summary":"The VFS spike's /do/{name}/ routes are served by the same Worker, unauthenticated","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819598Z","id":"5b408e78d25c21fc0f37e06b1bc3e6b3db316ef248a734ea646ab21a3192f98c","body":{"detail":"AppState's version comes from env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\") of crates/clax-worker, which is not the workspace's version (Cargo.toml [workspace.package] 0.4.0) and is not checked by scripts/check-version.sh.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":189},"content_hash":"5f3c9b04003a2773e3ae1df0627d16fbddc7c6084927c72a2bedd8f92964c90b"},"summary":"/healthz on the Worker reports version 0.0.0, the clax-worker crate's own version","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.901472Z","id":"53f0ce1492698c639a7d008bf7f253a03cb733d6380b9bfd9c7a0479fa5783e6","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":370},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"d143dd5ab7307c9179917744c58a2db137300422d33694b710645ac9772bb751"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"03b5bcf097345e4cc73a2057082676a8e6d2f762c6c5a20718d49fde001e6c89","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.909685Z","id":"5aa42a2994d40368602ec7681fdd48269780e4ca7d89faf0a53d4f77da00ee34","body":{"detail":"Measured under wrangler dev --local: POST /do/demo/fill?mb=4 wrote 1034 chunks in one commit in about 100 ms. Durable Object SQL bills per row written and caps a row at 2 MB, so a larger chunk (say 64 KiB, with PRAGMA page_size up to 65536) would cut rows and JS crossings for bulk writes at the cost of write amplification for small transactions. CHUNK_SIZE in crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs is the knob; measure with Clax's real write mix before changing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"ee1ef2163fd2f00ec4d1b73dbab1d0c9396f601127d0be89f8c574fc8f8469e9"},"summary":"Each commit runs one ctx.storage.sql.exec per 4 KiB chunk: a 4 MiB transaction is ~1034 statements and rows written","supersedes":"0fba429061d99ebf3bffe74f5beb9ff16c2e1ae5ba7b268f3e212d554b62a51f","tags":["vfs","performance","cost","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372362Z","id":"858d9c389d69624d1f79bbdbe92164601cab3171f11b1ff1aadb711dcdfb4185","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":537},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"547247babdee37802353717b998e69b11506b92e6dd0deb9f07ef8409e8ce811"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372407Z","id":"9989bf3d397e1d01eab733e455b6890aff3d1da34a40315697e1b928bf65104b","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"b352511c1c432e0bf20bbb5dc9a9283f1f260c8cc7d02632d0d7093eaed9ad02"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372441Z","id":"4d755683b7320abfda3b45d8f87f96418a92c6b5b3274ce20a4fbc9c23eebee4","body":{"detail":"A short or guessable CLAX_TOKEN secret makes the owner credential of a public Worker guessable; the generated one is 32 bytes of crypto.getRandomValues. A minimum length (32 characters) refused at start would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"285acd592c1778ae1830f3e175973b45eb0a303dc38e7716e58afa7ab8d7b0a8"},"summary":"CLAX_TOKEN is taken as the owner token whatever its length or entropy","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.750725Z","id":"0c5ebc3120df33df47e94a6bca20ecccf316f31079af2ff3a1022dd4f935810e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d81bf19","summary":"The Worker routes /do/ to the spike only with CLAX_TEST_ROUTES=1 (0 in wrangler.jsonc). Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs on a start with the checked-in variables prints 'ok   without test routes GET /do/wasm-test/stats is not the spike's', the same for POST /notes and /init, and 'ok   the plain start wrote nothing to the spike'.","supersedes":"6699046dc1f9b7ff717a8eb2406bf2e0f2bb96b7121915da9f60c957c653f3d5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.752873Z","id":"e7cf0a4de006c9cad07f197db823212805bf8e14395c331353098e228c96d54d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:874a9e5b","summary":"The alarm is set for the earliest due work (AppState::next_sweep_in, Store::grants_next_due, the planner refresh after a write), at least SWEEP_INTERVAL ahead, and deleted when nothing is due; the old set_alarm(now + 5 s) passed an absolute time where workers-rs takes an offset, so it never fired. Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs prints 'ok   with nothing due the object sets no alarm', 'ok   after a write the alarm is set for the planner refresh, an hour on', 'ok   with browsers open the alarm is set for the first presence or seat that lapses, not every few seconds' (alarm_live_ms 59745); cargo test -p clax-core next_lapse next_change grants_next_due passes.","supersedes":"559b60dd40fe42bb90375cc02208bcb68bb9eeb4295859960e2bd835acd43501","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.754870Z","id":"5e97e7dc64cf74420899c235202ce63d21f3a5c72bc6d4300de159168c1886c7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:af40f5d7","summary":"The instance serves with clax_server::VERSION. Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs summary reports \"version\":\"0.4.0\" from GET /healthz.","supersedes":"5b408e78d25c21fc0f37e06b1bc3e6b3db316ef248a734ea646ab21a3192f98c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:53.183235Z","id":"f1301565a6d7fb97831ef25029666b708a3860b6dad9618657934581557ff02b","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:a03f663c","references":"e7cf0a4de006c9cad07f197db823212805bf8e14395c331353098e228c96d54d","summary":"The commit that made this change is a03f663c (Set the instance's alarm for its next due work, and none when nothing is due); 874a9e5b named above is not on the branch.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.359181Z","id":"f3b86a6014ea55baa87d7e1d8b5801eacdb0f3f468ee3fcd1145b6d829030913","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"a3176f81a696b0033a0162647cdc4bf3440f1d7d9bbde2703b4d80447c29b633"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"03b5bcf097345e4cc73a2057082676a8e6d2f762c6c5a20718d49fde001e6c89","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:17:17.925016Z","id":"48a7f3fe8abccd9c82fa2723679c01776a7b97678923d2b0e8fd8e99cb28135e","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":297},"content_hash":"d143dd5ab7307c9179917744c58a2db137300422d33694b710645ac9772bb751"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"f3b86a6014ea55baa87d7e1d8b5801eacdb0f3f468ee3fcd1145b6d829030913","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.915702Z","id":"44f014aa4b4e8e00c83b784a895c38acc78c675c04d92b7fc7fa174cebc061c4","body":{"detail":"AppState::assemble takes StateParts::hosted (crates/clax-server/src/state.rs); the daemon passes cfg.hosted, the instance object None. Hosted mode on the Worker needs: a Hosted built from the Worker's vars (public origin and its Host, the setup secret as a Worker secret, behind_cloudflare true, since every request carries CF-Connecting-IP); hosted::gate's Host check against that public host, while the router's self_base is PUBLIC_ORIGIN; the MCP adapter's allowed hosts (routes/mcp_http.rs allowed_hosts) built from self_base's authority, so a public /mcp works only when PUBLIC_ORIGIN names the host agents call; a content origin for artifacts other than <id>.localhost (the crate docs of crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs); and reopening woken sockets with the guest flag: routes::stream::open_stream takes guest, and the instance passes false at crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:334 because identity::SocketCredentials does not carry it, so a hosted guest's socket rebuilt after hibernation would stop carrying drafts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"f3e6f3b45115fbe6912d51d12d6c38852e6279b20fa4595516a8c31fbf85b4a2"},"summary":"The Worker builds its state with hosted: None, so the hosted gate, sign-in routes, per-person rights and guests' drafts are off on it","tags":["worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.915906Z","id":"d469194dc01f8665c05426c0744154c3bedeea5e23c7d24eaece92719a2af182","body":{"detail":"Seen once per POST /api/artifacts in crates/clax-worker/target/e2e/run-*/wrangler-1.log after commit cfe9fdaa; the publish answers 201 and the e2e passes. InstanceDo::fetch converts the runtime Request to an HttpRequest (HttpRequest::try_from), whose body is the runtime's stream re-wrapped; crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs's entry and repos::worker::forward_git take the runtime Request as it is for that reason. A body read or cancelled after the router answered (a body limit layer, or the body dropped late) would throw this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":502},"end":{"line":507},"content_hash":"fc239eb8256637ec09f907e1cd7a0de309aee5bcc9a9d78c7bbf2a418d1c6178"},"summary":"A publish to the instance object logs 'Uncaught TypeError: Can't read from request stream after response has been sent' in wrangler","tags":["worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.916290Z","id":"e0ff2c0d12ffb3cdf2cdfd06e7594de21bceea3403cc711534c25a2f426d972d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"152eccb222f89af0b7eb19d266d222468db35a878ba2f2c285525679eab009ae","summary":"Since the merge of hosted sign-in (cb3495e7) the server has hosted mode, but the Worker still passes StateParts::hosted None; what hosted mode on the Worker needs is listed on the concern at crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:242:245.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.916367Z","id":"c5f362ac7f6470c0b7465f26edaa071fe191b5c275b5228705ad835549589491","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"14d2d0a067f2f8a886782f40f2effacba9d06ebd3b697e539ef4fe45789e35f7","summary":"Since ccf75bd5 the Worker serves /mcp through the JSON-RPC adapter (routes::mcp_http, clax_mcp::http). Drafts' idle sweep now runs from the alarm (AppState::sweep, Drafts::next_idle in next_sweep_in, 06f59a8e). Still not served: the live-layers socket (concern at crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:467:479).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.916515Z","id":"2a2e66b6cefccb2dc37a07790238be69070448a86f75f26a7e2263134447e440","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cfe9fdaa","summary":"DoContent is removed in cfe9fdaa: the instance object keeps versions in git (RepoDO or Cloudflare Artifacts) and assets in R2 through repos::worker::content_store. git show cfe9fdaa --stat lists crates/clax-worker/src/content.rs deleted; node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs passes on the git store.","supersedes":"b36a16b82268f582575348b72709054d2c51eb2fbc81b04f1b7e0836670dc25b","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.898100Z","id":"0ca7ace461a4034fe9a0e8fa7ace71024addc1004b66bd09d3436533a755d473","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:529dad9c","summary":"With HOSTED=1 the instance builds Hosted from PUBLIC_ORIGIN, CONTENT_ORIGIN and the SETUP_SECRET secret, behind Cloudflare (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted). Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs prints 'ok   the first person sets up with the secret and sees the gallery', 'ok   Sam joins with the invite in a second browser', 'ok   the sign-in link signs a third browser in as Sam', 'ok   Sam mints an agent token whose command names the public /mcp', 'ok   the guest comments' and exits 0 (43 checks).","supersedes":"44f014aa4b4e8e00c83b784a895c38acc78c675c04d92b7fc7fa174cebc061c4","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.902605Z","id":"951646067b26e79292ba24012a3f8b58fced5c346464f51adff5a11a7ccc9119","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:529dad9c","summary":"A hosted instance (HOSTED=1) replaces the local semantics: browsers sign in as the owner, people and guests through the hosted gate. Without HOSTED the Worker keeps the token-owner rules, as documented in crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs's module docs. Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs exits 0, its owner browser holding the owner's surfaces (People, invites, sharing by link).","supersedes":"152eccb222f89af0b7eb19d266d222468db35a878ba2f2c285525679eab009ae","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.906924Z","id":"463b5e1bce299d97efc00a967b6fdd31b35c567338e47fab2cec0cb9880c635c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:529dad9c","summary":"InstanceDo::fetch reads the body whole before routing (instance.rs http_request) instead of HttpRequest::try_from's stream. Evidence: after node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs (which publishes), grep -c 'request stream' on its wrangler-1.log and wrangler-2.log prints 0 for each, where the same e2e's logs on the base commit 897022bd carried the TypeError.","supersedes":"d469194dc01f8665c05426c0744154c3bedeea5e23c7d24eaece92719a2af182","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.947641Z","id":"14390babed4f7f3352e5ccbaa3e5c6153e15adf5005a595edfdbfb5b8384a23e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"14d2d0a067f2f8a886782f40f2effacba9d06ebd3b697e539ef4fe45789e35f7","summary":"Since 529dad9c and 77bb5c7f the Worker serves the room and live-layers sockets (hibernatable, reopened after a wake), runs question graces from the alarm (questions::SweptGraces), and keeps live seats and presence across a wake. Still not run on the Worker: the session reaper (a hosted agent's adapter session, registered by crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs bearer_session, ends only when its token is revoked).","tags":["worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.948018Z","id":"0b74d13096756eaf095acb560bb3a3228b6d8204e32ecd9d389608e2fa42b513","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":514},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.142823Z","id":"f1d81745f9a1e1712d43397aca2a10bb09aa672f472518c9eb8ccc747e012164","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":393},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"cd2c6d54792a75b527e0ebfd70f39ab3a684536b4be6e53f5a781674cc2c277e"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"53f0ce1492698c639a7d008bf7f253a03cb733d6380b9bfd9c7a0479fa5783e6","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.147276Z","id":"64f2e13d2d9a6b9bb930e91a95a062db82269d89f5b594c1a78095664ca8e2a6","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"549861f15c2184c08e14b20fe2e555af5816030924991dd9487527b43462e73b"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"48a7f3fe8abccd9c82fa2723679c01776a7b97678923d2b0e8fd8e99cb28135e","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.353833Z","id":"707b77a8e4fbae081b3731254c9b59513ab793e0aa00897ec1ac20531588030b","body":{"detail":"Not served on the Worker: GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/room (the room capability's socket; routes/room.rs is native only and its frames ride per-room tokio broadcast receivers that need a drain of their own, see 61069320), /mcp (the JSON-RPC adapter of crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs, not built), GET /api/events (SSE). Not run: the session reaper (daemon::reap_idle checks local PIDs), the stale check and the audit journal. Still on a timer: a question's grace (questions::start_grace, see dfae291e), which keeps the object awake and is lost at eviction. After a wake the hub, live seats and presence start empty: each socket gets a new stream and the shell subscribes again, so seats are taken again in that order and presence chips disappear until tabs report (102650cd). There is no live-layers socket on this base to carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"14c4789f25debfd1554c7cb73a86f5a6e66635cbcbdb34f728850922fab70200"},"summary":"What the daemon runs that the Worker does not: rooms, /mcp, the session reaper, question graces on a timer, live seats and presence across a wake","supersedes":"14d2d0a067f2f8a886782f40f2effacba9d06ebd3b697e539ef4fe45789e35f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.358698Z","id":"ded8878041f92e2624d114599834401082137ff8e51dba688c09ee3bb0a8a433","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"600dd0ea2618052984d2503af9cce895580a8e46338c01b2c421c8e4645d0d1b"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"9989bf3d397e1d01eab733e455b6890aff3d1da34a40315697e1b928bf65104b","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.363545Z","id":"d34e48c352e4c42a25245070a3e047a65e90bc9440e3b43332f36841ef2d14b4","body":{"detail":"A short or guessable CLAX_TOKEN secret makes the owner credential of a public Worker guessable; the generated one is 32 bytes of crypto.getRandomValues. A minimum length (32 characters) refused at start would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":297},"content_hash":"5fc56972eb931aa596d72b4a21538bf53a5803bfb74c4ee35b4550a68f003403"},"summary":"CLAX_TOKEN is taken as the owner token whatever its length or entropy","supersedes":"4d755683b7320abfda3b45d8f87f96418a92c6b5b3274ce20a4fbc9c23eebee4","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.368408Z","id":"1787166cc02bc8960b4b0373e73d9b896a3ce681a2f352374c238ddb7344d9a9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":963},"end":{"line":991},"content_hash":"5aefb4815a0b2a2c1254b9bc338f015fb3eb1f1c0ced47cf0fcfa12b6e8ee47c"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"858d9c389d69624d1f79bbdbe92164601cab3171f11b1ff1aadb711dcdfb4185","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:21:25.590854Z","id":"69829535fefda89ac12152f1438e24e041c823c83fd04f90c8110f6a44acdbc7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1004},"end":{"line":1032},"content_hash":"5aefb4815a0b2a2c1254b9bc338f015fb3eb1f1c0ced47cf0fcfa12b6e8ee47c"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"1787166cc02bc8960b4b0373e73d9b896a3ce681a2f352374c238ddb7344d9a9","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:01:07.848492Z","id":"d403fb03a09fc2ef0392abe3ccf0d6c0f88aae2a303d4181374439ca9f805846","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"707b77a8e4fbae081b3731254c9b59513ab793e0aa00897ec1ac20531588030b","summary":"Since 878d299f a hosted agent's adapter sessions are those of crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs serve_agent (one per initialize, answered as Mcp-Session-Id), not bearer_session's mcp:<grant>, which the merge did not take. On the Worker, where the reaper does not run, such a session ends when its client sends DELETE, when its token is revoked, or when the token's sessions pass Store::BEARER_SESSION_CAP (the least recently seen ends).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053564Z","id":"95401e57086d366018d44e3037ec6d74ca69345b51c0aa2e0f9724d57a8b1e64","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"7c74baf9324959c5095b468825f50da06da93eab879c036edea5a0b8c31c0998"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.350224Z","id":"df3fe77ccf2b383e4ed76591a98c907a718e412c50d4177fccd32bb073ac4ed3","body":{"detail":"AppState::assemble takes StateParts::hosted (crates/clax-server/src/state.rs); the daemon passes cfg.hosted, the instance object None. Hosted mode on the Worker needs: a Hosted built from the Worker's vars (public origin and its Host, the setup secret as a Worker secret, behind_cloudflare true, since every request carries CF-Connecting-IP); hosted::gate's Host check against that public host, while the router's self_base is PUBLIC_ORIGIN; the MCP adapter's allowed hosts (routes/mcp_http.rs allowed_hosts) built from self_base's authority, so a public /mcp works only when PUBLIC_ORIGIN names the host agents call; a content origin for artifacts other than <id>.localhost (the crate docs of crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs); and reopening woken sockets with the guest flag: routes::stream::open_stream takes guest, and the instance passes false at crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:334 because identity::SocketCredentials does not carry it, so a hosted guest's socket rebuilt after hibernation would stop carrying drafts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":251},"end":{"line":254},"content_hash":"f3e6f3b45115fbe6912d51d12d6c38852e6279b20fa4595516a8c31fbf85b4a2"},"summary":"The Worker builds its state with hosted: None, so the hosted gate, sign-in routes, per-person rights and guests' drafts are off on it","supersedes":"44f014aa4b4e8e00c83b784a895c38acc78c675c04d92b7fc7fa174cebc061c4","tags":["worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.374160Z","id":"a527647bbb21ab870d993bf9129d867c0087faafffe36a196ed791deb5582f93","body":{"detail":"Seen once per POST /api/artifacts in crates/clax-worker/target/e2e/run-*/wrangler-1.log after commit cfe9fdaa; the publish answers 201 and the e2e passes. InstanceDo::fetch converts the runtime Request to an HttpRequest (HttpRequest::try_from), whose body is the runtime's stream re-wrapped; crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs's entry and repos::worker::forward_git take the runtime Request as it is for that reason. A body read or cancelled after the router answered (a body limit layer, or the body dropped late) would throw this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":511},"end":{"line":529},"content_hash":"1252ba65269bd47f1de9676862f53d40e865727abdd3451bc58c150d3471d7ab"},"summary":"A publish to the instance object logs 'Uncaught TypeError: Can't read from request stream after response has been sent' in wrangler","supersedes":"d469194dc01f8665c05426c0744154c3bedeea5e23c7d24eaece92719a2af182","tags":["worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.378431Z","id":"c9c1925f9d788f06213df4cd9e822f512e7f3e8c62032dc5490017a06dd65f0a","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"39aa8c71d500ab303c71c00c468e696db4759eabe819f9eefbecf45d559d465e"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"95401e57086d366018d44e3037ec6d74ca69345b51c0aa2e0f9724d57a8b1e64","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:34:05.507455Z","id":"e3e78fb21263664ecf667c6fc0b2594e0b11df882b59c1855c40f9e3a3412a41","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c9c1925f9d788f06213df4cd9e822f512e7f3e8c62032dc5490017a06dd65f0a","summary":"Since c1a739d2 the consumer acknowledges a reconcile the instance refuses (4xx: a malformed call or an ID that is no artifact's), which a retry cannot change, and retries only failures (5xx, a failed fetch), at most max_retries (3) times per wrangler.jsonc; there is no dead-letter queue, so a message that keeps failing is dropped after its retries.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.746658Z","id":"1579f370731c4f8f8bad5cc56db23ceac0cb4def97e99b9e43150c29fefbf783","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"df3fe77ccf2b383e4ed76591a98c907a718e412c50d4177fccd32bb073ac4ed3","summary":"The git token routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/git_token.rs) serve the owner by token and agent sessions here; until hosted mode is on, no browser on the Worker is a person, so the shell's Clone is offered only to a browser presenting the owner token (crates/clax-worker/e2e-clone.mjs).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.062645Z","id":"e2d2214a9cbb9f1423a57ac61c16e7d5eb855c6d0ac651e97246ce39023719ca","body":{"detail":"Not served on the Worker: GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/room (the room capability's socket; routes/room.rs is native only and its frames ride per-room tokio broadcast receivers that need a drain of their own, see 61069320), /mcp (the JSON-RPC adapter of crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs, not built), GET /api/events (SSE). Not run: the session reaper (daemon::reap_idle checks local PIDs), the stale check and the audit journal. Still on a timer: a question's grace (questions::start_grace, see dfae291e), which keeps the object awake and is lost at eviction. After a wake the hub, live seats and presence start empty: each socket gets a new stream and the shell subscribes again, so seats are taken again in that order and presence chips disappear until tabs report (102650cd). There is no live-layers socket on this base to carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"000d0f3013c210b40770539e5b273052b5a1faba119f8b310030871ad273557e"},"summary":"What the daemon runs that the Worker does not: rooms, /mcp, the session reaper, question graces on a timer, live seats and presence across a wake","supersedes":"14d2d0a067f2f8a886782f40f2effacba9d06ebd3b697e539ef4fe45789e35f7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.067033Z","id":"5498dd86239fcb3950588b4a62b644c2f0bd3a16f43bf608d24213346e27955b","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"72731f5fdcd2322729205c8acb5c5be9e20a6e260e7041c989d2f81aef3698c5"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"9989bf3d397e1d01eab733e455b6890aff3d1da34a40315697e1b928bf65104b","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.071536Z","id":"daa9d9b0e793a37ebf0f238c21aab3f3f3ad435ffbd222725b973665c8f9cc6c","body":{"detail":"A short or guessable CLAX_TOKEN secret makes the owner credential of a public Worker guessable; the generated one is 32 bytes of crypto.getRandomValues. A minimum length (32 characters) refused at start would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"1b160f47605d376bbb7cc394a9fee91fa1bff040aaf0efa41de1855ce53a2392"},"summary":"CLAX_TOKEN is taken as the owner token whatever its length or entropy","supersedes":"4d755683b7320abfda3b45d8f87f96418a92c6b5b3274ce20a4fbc9c23eebee4","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.076042Z","id":"6a0dbd2ed22884f6fb611bb464def75014ea5b3dbe708c6bba68282aa00db106","body":{"detail":"With conn_of None (crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs), GET /api/token answers 403 not_loopback and the owner and events cookies never count, so the owner is only whoever presents CLAX_TOKEN as a bearer token (scripts, agents), never a browser. Anyone who reaches the Worker gets a clax_viewer cookie and, as on a daemon bound to the LAN, reads every artifact and comments (people are not filtered: feedback::VisFor). bind is 127.0.0.1 here, so invites answer 409 not_on_lan; browser_base and self_base are PUBLIC_ORIGIN or http://localhost; codex push, sampling and the audit journal are off; extension_id is empty, so the Chrome extension cannot pair. What hosted mode (the rust-hosted-signin branch) must change: a sign-in that makes a browser the owner or a person (an owner credential that does not depend on the peer), refusing anonymous viewers on a public deploy, invites without a LAN address, and the public host as browser_base.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"6b2fbd72662f5a1df345e30b32c622952abadfbb4dcb483410ac44431f2b30d7"},"summary":"On the Worker every browser is a LAN viewer and no browser can become the owner: hosted mode must replace these local semantics","supersedes":"152eccb222f89af0b7eb19d266d222468db35a878ba2f2c285525679eab009ae","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.080392Z","id":"2290e47638b7cbed716c86dc4fc95a0b40db38258461484745ff27d7448d3228","body":{"detail":"AppState::assemble takes StateParts::hosted (crates/clax-server/src/state.rs); the daemon passes cfg.hosted, the instance object None. Hosted mode on the Worker needs: a Hosted built from the Worker's vars (public origin and its Host, the setup secret as a Worker secret, behind_cloudflare true, since every request carries CF-Connecting-IP); hosted::gate's Host check against that public host, while the router's self_base is PUBLIC_ORIGIN; the MCP adapter's allowed hosts (routes/mcp_http.rs allowed_hosts) built from self_base's authority, so a public /mcp works only when PUBLIC_ORIGIN names the host agents call; a content origin for artifacts other than <id>.localhost (the crate docs of crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs); and reopening woken sockets with the guest flag: routes::stream::open_stream takes guest, and the instance passes false at crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs:334 because identity::SocketCredentials does not carry it, so a hosted guest's socket rebuilt after hibernation would stop carrying drafts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":266},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"f3e6f3b45115fbe6912d51d12d6c38852e6279b20fa4595516a8c31fbf85b4a2"},"summary":"The Worker builds its state with hosted: None, so the hosted gate, sign-in routes, per-person rights and guests' drafts are off on it","supersedes":"df3fe77ccf2b383e4ed76591a98c907a718e412c50d4177fccd32bb073ac4ed3","tags":["worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.084768Z","id":"24f78763876946882ed90299e80b06c81ce33b7f053ac2a153dfd01732e9b0ad","body":{"detail":"Seen once per POST /api/artifacts in crates/clax-worker/target/e2e/run-*/wrangler-1.log after commit cfe9fdaa; the publish answers 201 and the e2e passes. InstanceDo::fetch converts the runtime Request to an HttpRequest (HttpRequest::try_from), whose body is the runtime's stream re-wrapped; crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs's entry and repos::worker::forward_git take the runtime Request as it is for that reason. A body read or cancelled after the router answered (a body limit layer, or the body dropped late) would throw this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":527},"end":{"line":545},"content_hash":"1252ba65269bd47f1de9676862f53d40e865727abdd3451bc58c150d3471d7ab"},"summary":"A publish to the instance object logs 'Uncaught TypeError: Can't read from request stream after response has been sent' in wrangler","supersedes":"a527647bbb21ab870d993bf9129d867c0087faafffe36a196ed791deb5582f93","tags":["worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.089197Z","id":"8ff1253101ed32377473c836c3d87e9967132d3de60eef18e187c14851001dd9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":553},"end":{"line":581},"content_hash":"adde13b66df2c66267aa835cb38a60fc31920d3f6d36b2a1e7bbc2c0fbd425a0"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"858d9c389d69624d1f79bbdbe92164601cab3171f11b1ff1aadb711dcdfb4185","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231454Z","id":"934bb3b5f8c14d19f77bc1d1235f3ed680953d9b7a96398e0f46fa8f71c6412f","body":{"detail":"Per developers.cloudflare.com/queues/event-subscriptions/events-schemas (Artifacts). Nothing subscribes each artifact's repository a-<ID>, so on a deploy the consumer receives no pushed event and a push to Artifacts becomes a version only at the artifact's next publish (the reconcile before each publish). crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs subscribes its own artifact's repository while it runs, so its push step exercises this consumer; making a subscription per repository needs the Cloudflare API from the Worker (an API token secret), which the Worker does not have.","kind":"comment","references":"c9c1925f9d788f06213df4cd9e822f512e7f3e8c62032dc5490017a06dd65f0a","summary":"Artifacts sends cf.artifacts.repo.pushed only to a subscription on one repository (source artifacts.repo with --source-namespace and --source-repo-name, wrangler 4.149.0 and later); the account-wide source artifacts carries only repo.created/deleted/forked/imported","tags":["artifacts","queues","deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231806Z","id":"85e08670564c4aa5ea718f451860a5902fc57d32ff53257f33e590cc8a840269","body":{"detail":"The routes are gated only by CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES and the CLAX_TOKEN secret (compared whole, same_secret). Their power is within the owner's, but a leaked CLAX_TOKEN gains repository write tokens that the server's routes would not hand out. deploy.mjs (CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES: o.diag) and its closing steps tell the owner to redeploy with --no-diag once the smoke is green; nothing enforces it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"64cfa5d0da9306a78a0dbbaebd2d6b2cd59ed7c1ba86f1a0c281f10195bc0134"},"suggested_fix":"Default to off once a deploy's smoke has passed, or expire the routes (e.g. a CLAX_DIAG_UNTIL timestamp var deploy.mjs sets an hour ahead).","summary":"deploy.mjs deploys with CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES=1 unless --no-diag: the owner token can then create and delete clax-diag-* Artifacts repositories and mint write tokens for any artifact's repository","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:35:27.964822Z","id":"e303ab6b22c64b0373a7d5b630468fcac271a6654b2d336d9612ff340fe00394","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"c9c1925f9d788f06213df4cd9e822f512e7f3e8c62032dc5490017a06dd65f0a","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:35:27.969398Z","id":"845d7d0c76e5e310eeb109d583b12c0f4e498589e64e92bdabe93c3805da56d7","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":329},"content_hash":"098458e33abcea3403097eec93387b9a5da3e534f917272dca1328cff80e5e99"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"64f2e13d2d9a6b9bb930e91a95a062db82269d89f5b594c1a78095664ca8e2a6","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.034027Z","id":"916ea85fa9b75a7defc0240f933490084e95d5f1f055941b8fadaa2d48ffefbc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:27a48a40","summary":"deploy.mjs now deploys with CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES=0 unless --diag, which prints a reminder to deploy again without it; smoke-remote.mjs ends with the same reminder when a deployed Worker still answers /_diag/. Evidence: node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com --no-build prints 'diagnostics off' and wrangler.deploy.jsonc holds \"CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES\": \"0\"; with --diag it prints 'THE DIAGNOSTICS ROUTES ARE ON'.","supersedes":"85e08670564c4aa5ea718f451860a5902fc57d32ff53257f33e590cc8a840269","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"4c4d70000dbc6cb6c32db6ad482bb0c1dcc60aae81f1e282c73f72fc1f212753","body":{"detail":"The DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so the expect() calls are the only way to report failure. A production object should keep the open error and answer every request with it (or retry the open lazily), so a transient storage error does not poison the object.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":332},"content_hash":"098458e33abcea3403097eec93387b9a5da3e534f917272dca1328cff80e5e99"},"summary":"ClaxDb::new panics if the VFS tables or the database cannot be opened, leaving the object unusable until the isolate restarts","supersedes":"845d7d0c76e5e310eeb109d583b12c0f4e498589e64e92bdabe93c3805da56d7","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"b28aefa0d27ccfdbc3af5f7764cc250ec71d4a9658efb15fef8e80e1fbe25da7","body":{"detail":"last_optimize starts at construction and wrote at false, so each eviction restarts the hour and forgets the write. Keeping the time of the last refresh in the _clax_instance table would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":237},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"600dd0ea2618052984d2503af9cce895580a8e46338c01b2c421c8e4645d0d1b"},"summary":"The planner refresh's clock and the 'a request wrote' flag live in memory: an object evicted within the hour after each write never refreshes the planner","supersedes":"ded8878041f92e2624d114599834401082137ff8e51dba688c09ee3bb0a8a433","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ea1ccd0aafebd1bd1971c26c3397298cc29700e46860c38593a32f5b6789d73a","body":{"detail":"A short or guessable CLAX_TOKEN secret makes the owner credential of a public Worker guessable; the generated one is 32 bytes of crypto.getRandomValues. A minimum length (32 characters) refused at start would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":310},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"5fc56972eb931aa596d72b4a21538bf53a5803bfb74c4ee35b4550a68f003403"},"summary":"CLAX_TOKEN is taken as the owner token whatever its length or entropy","supersedes":"d34e48c352e4c42a25245070a3e047a65e90bc9440e3b43332f36841ef2d14b4","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"88fb1340c164848f494f4c3c7b60a73969a0ff7f93b0537c2c85ef20e99761e1","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":541},"end":{"line":555},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"0b74d13096756eaf095acb560bb3a3228b6d8204e32ecd9d389608e2fa42b513","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"bdac5d459d7667cbb74e7eb835ac219e79779552360b22239214ee14e880c471","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"e303ab6b22c64b0373a7d5b630468fcac271a6654b2d336d9612ff340fe00394","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.943215Z","id":"9eacb267a2a5b02befcc9e3fda0f2de23ca5c11fc45e52738c7ccbc6e36f31a5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that 0ca7ace461a4034fe9a0e8fa7ace71024addc1004b66bd09d3436533a755d473 closed (With HOSTED=1 the instance builds Hosted from PUBLIC_ORIGIN, CONTENT_ORIGIN and the SETUP_SECRET secret, behind Cloudflare (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs f). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"2290e47638b7cbed716c86dc4fc95a0b40db38258461484745ff27d7448d3228","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.950211Z","id":"a5574e1d033180b39c28610a600a970791cd37ee032ad24c08371d618a717bd4","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that 951646067b26e79292ba24012a3f8b58fced5c346464f51adff5a11a7ccc9119 closed (A hosted instance (HOSTED=1) replaces the local semantics: browsers sign in as the owner, people and guests through the hosted gate. Without HOSTED the Worker k). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"6a0dbd2ed22884f6fb611bb464def75014ea5b3dbe708c6bba68282aa00db106","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.957335Z","id":"05cb2b7300a761ce3e84bc2102d4736ffebc8fbf081b3b3b77336360fcd792ad","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that 463b5e1bce299d97efc00a967b6fdd31b35c567338e47fab2cec0cb9880c635c closed (InstanceDo::fetch reads the body whole before routing (instance.rs http_request) instead of HttpRequest::try_from's stream. Evidence: after node crates/clax-wor). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"24f78763876946882ed90299e80b06c81ce33b7f053ac2a153dfd01732e9b0ad","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
