{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.177500Z","id":"04dd1caa37345a5305226112e7a8e5d3c99be61bfb8059cd7ee51caa452bd057","body":{"detail":"Instance::keep serializes every held seat and live presence report and writes the JSON to _clax_instance when it differs from the last write: each presence report (every tab, about every 30 s) moves a timestamp, so each costs one row write, and the row grows with the artifacts open (64 people by 16 tabs per artifact at most for presence, the seat limits for seats). Rows per artifact, or writing only seat and presence changes a viewer could see, would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"3490fdde295826c3fbfaf630af2fd8574f534c487f17b9628fb69bb50dbc4b23"},"summary":"The kept seats and presence are rewritten whole in the object's storage after every event that changed them, presence PUTs included","supersedes":"7ea92c989319c4b77e43fff1a1028788ec70fa9e6dcc0eca9b60a6f8ffd70f62","tags":["worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.239530Z","id":"b3f8aae3cd62bb0adcb7f88b3ea25e4e2ba1e067c3b276a6d7d912bdcb419146","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs reads the alarm through GET /_worker/alarm, but every due time is a minute or more away (presence 90 s, stream grace 60 s, seat idle, grant expiry, planner refresh 1 h), so the alarm handler's sweep, grant expiry and optimize never run under test. A test route that runs the handler now, or due times shortened by test variables, would cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1227},"end":{"line":1245},"content_hash":"b3759215a701feeed46b3294339746437bc38573d48d3ecfc07d9aad5027b033"},"summary":"No test fires the instance's alarm: the e2e checks only when it is set","supersedes":"9bd4da41d68c748101444b2706597735df1bca8786e14c67f66ba225e45f3b19","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.269308Z","id":"32ae62783cfd53d82c8c8b5adede71e8fffd2eb5442e6cb45c6e664780b50f42","body":{"detail":"queue plans each batch with clax_git::events::plan_batch and asks the instance to reconcile each named artifact, acking on 200 and retrying otherwise. Under wrangler dev --local the queue is simulated and receives no Artifacts event, and no test delivers a batch to it: the event body's shape (clax_git::events::event_repo) and the consumer's ack/retry are unverified. The queue clax-artifacts-events and the event subscription must be created on the account before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"1c08828df7803969a798a8113dc5ec971873781f1fac611c145cc908494efc6a"},"summary":"The Artifacts pushed-event queue consumer has never run against Cloudflare Queues or a real Artifacts event","supersedes":"bdac5d459d7667cbb74e7eb835ac219e79779552360b22239214ee14e880c471","tags":["revisit:a Cloudflare account with Artifacts and Queues is available","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537078Z","id":"4a8bb2d935ba0b2a0a12a635c827c1b42ff2b83c762c04b709bce74179259b42","body":{"detail":"The Worker embeds web/dist with rust-embed for the state's web tree (the artifact page and gallery the router renders), as clax-server's own embed did before the web UI left it. clax-embedded also carries the extension, the plugin trees and the marketplaces, and its build script needs their directories; the Worker serves none of them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"bcdd04ddb9008ee6be7eb120f962bdbb05d3658429d4fdebff1767f26473853b"},"summary":"Link clax-embedded in the Worker instead of embedding web/dist itself","tags":["worker","layout","revisit:clax-embedded splits its web UI from the other embeds","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223495Z","id":"b7f82e10fc5a859ea4bace5afc75540c9d76cfdc1548ed3f4c5d871d99b9e4ee","body":{"detail":"same_secret (lines 33-40) gates the /_diag/ routes on the owner's CLAX_TOKEN (line 193). It reimplements clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq, which crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:703 and crates/clax-server/src/github.rs:95 use for the same job. base64 (lines 69-86) reimplements standard padded base64, though crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml:28 already depends on base64 0.22. A third copy of the comparison means a fix to the shared one does not reach the diag gate.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"df5e7c87c0aa121e7170cfb1e69120a0c5bce010f6a8e51749551f9093a64f95"},"suggested_fix":"Replace same_secret with clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq(presented.as_bytes(), token.as_bytes()), and base64() with base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD.encode. Then drop both helpers and their tests (lines 814-825).","summary":"diag.rs hand-rolls a constant-time comparison and a base64 encoder that the workspace already provides","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507749Z","id":"16cb8463842ccc3c116d044a37928e792a4566c026f20356561f3ed179ef876e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs:33-40 same_secret is byte-for-byte the body of crates/clax-core/src/secret.rs:74-79 constant_time_eq (pub, in pub mod secret, crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs:42); it gates /_diag/ at diag.rs:193. crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:703 and crates/clax-server/src/github.rs:95 call the shared one. diag.rs:69-86 hand-rolls padded standard base64; crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml:28 depends on base64 0.22 and crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs:29-30 already uses its engine. clax-core is a dependency of clax-worker (Cargo.toml:31). Minor: diag.rs holds a second copy of the comparison, not a third. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"b7f82e10fc5a859ea4bace5afc75540c9d76cfdc1548ed3f4c5d871d99b9e4ee","summary":"confirmed: same_secret and base64 duplicate clax_core::secret::constant_time_eq and the base64 crate the worker already depends on","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
